/// Year 5 Humanities's Term 8: "Age of Exploration and Trade Routes" --
/// following the Silk Road overland (Week 29) and Indian Ocean maritime
/// (Week 29) trade networks that once linked distant civilisations, the
/// term turns to the Age of Discovery (Week 30), examining the
/// navigational inventions -- the compass, the astrolabe, the caravel --
/// and the famous explorers -- Columbus, Vasco da Gama, Magellan -- who
/// used them to cross uncharted oceans. Week 31 zooms into the practical
/// skill of cartography itself: reading grid references, compass roses,
/// and legends, and understanding how early world maps left blank spaces
/// where the world was not yet mapped. Week 32 closes the term with a
/// capstone, "The Nova School Explorers' Fair", in which students
/// explicitly combine all three threads -- Silk Road trade knowledge from
/// Week 29, the explorers and their inventions from Week 30, and the
/// cartography skills from Week 31 -- into one running story: an
/// explorer logbook and a hand-drawn route map showing a single
/// character's journey by both overland caravan and sailing ship.
