        passageEn:
            "Moe Moe's aunt travels around Myanmar for her job, and every time she visits a new region or state, she sends Moe Moe a postcard describing what makes that place special.\n\nThe first postcard comes from Rakhine State, describing long sandy beaches along the Bay of Bengal. The second comes from Shan State, describing cool hills, tea plantations, and fishermen rowing with their legs on Inle Lake. The third comes from Kachin State, describing snow-capped mountains far in the north, colder than anywhere else Moe Moe has heard of in Myanmar. The fourth comes from Mon State, describing ancient golden pagodas along the southern coast.\n\nMoe Moe pins all four postcards on her bedroom wall next to a map of Myanmar, drawing a line from each postcard to where it belongs on the map. As she looks at her wall, she realizes that Myanmar stretches from icy mountain peaks in the north all the way to warm sandy coastlines in the south, with cool highland lakes in between.\n\nHer aunt tells her that no two regions or states are exactly alike, and that is what makes traveling around Myanmar so exciting -- there is always somewhere new and different to discover.",
