        passageEn:
            "Zaw Zaw's family grew extra mangoes in their garden, so his mother let him set up a small stall at the market to sell them. \"Each mango costs 500 kyats,\" his mother told him, helping him write the price on a small sign.\n\n"
            "Soon, a customer approached and picked up two mangoes. \"That will be 1000 kyats, please,\" Zaw Zaw said politely, feeling proud to be a seller for the first time. The customer handed him a 2000-kyat note.\n\n"
            "Zaw Zaw thought carefully. \"2000 minus 1000 is 1000,\" he calculated, handing back exactly 1000 kyats in change. The customer smiled and thanked him for the fair transaction, walking away happily with their mangoes.\n\n"
            "By the end of the day, Zaw Zaw had sold nearly all his mangoes and counted his earnings carefully with his mother. \"Being a seller means setting fair prices and giving correct change,\" he told his friends the next day. \"It's harder than it looks, but I really enjoyed it!\"",
        passageMy:
