        passageEn:
            "One day, their teacher was away, and a substitute teacher forgot to remind the class about the usual rules. Without anyone raising their hand, several students started shouting answers at once, making it impossible to hear anyone clearly.\n\n"
            "Zaw Zaw tried to walk to the pencil sharpener, but two other students bumped into him because nobody was lining up properly. \"This is so confusing,\" he said, feeling frustrated by the noise and disorder.\n\n"
            "Nay Chi noticed that without the usual quiet-voice rule, she couldn't concentrate on her reading at all. \"I can't hear myself think,\" she said, covering her ears from the noise around her.\n\n"
            "When their regular teacher returned the next day and reminded the class of their usual rules, everyone quickly settled back into an organized, fair, and quiet classroom. \"Now I understand why we have rules,\" said Moe Moe. \"They're not there to make things boring. They're there to help everyone learn and feel safe.\"",
